{"openapi": "3.1.0", "info": {"title": "mendel-api", "summary": "The forge and Mendel, over one schema.", "description": "**The schema is the contract.** `frontend/src/api/` is generated from this document and never hand-edited, and an agent driving Mendel reads the same document \u2014 so an operation without an `operationId`, a tag, or a declared refusal is a gap in both consumers at once.", "version": "0.1.0"}, "paths": {"/api/health": {"get": {"tags": ["health"], "summary": "Is the service up", "description": "Liveness only. What the *registry* looks like is `/health/registry`, which walks\na directory \u2014 conflating the two makes a liveness probe do real work.", "operationId": "liveness", "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"additionalProperties": {"type": "boolean"}, "type": "object", "title": "Response Liveness"}}}}}}}, "/api/questions": {"get": {"tags": ["questions"], "summary": "Every open question, filtered, ordered and collapsed", "description": "The queue.\n\n**Every control is a query parameter and none of them is a header or a body**, because a\ncurator who finds a bad answer must be able to send somebody the link to the screen they\nwere looking at \u2014 spec \u00a74.1.", "operationId": "listQuestions", "parameters": [{"name": "band", "in": "query", "required": false, "schema": {"anyOf": [{"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Band"}, {"type": "null"}], "description": "Only this band.", "title": "Band"}, "description": "Only this band."}, {"name": "group", "in": "query", "required": false, "schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Grouping", "description": "One row per question, or per draft.", "default": "question"}, "description": "One row per question, or per draft."}, {"name": "sort", "in": "query", "required": false, "schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Ordering", "description": "Worst-to-get-wrong, or newest.", "default": "consequence"}, "description": "Worst-to-get-wrong, or newest."}, {"name": "since_last_visit", "in": "query", "required": false, "schema": {"type": "boolean", "description": "Only what moved since you last looked.", "default": false, "title": "Since Last Visit"}, "description": "Only what moved since you last looked."}], "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/QueueResponse"}}}}, "422": {"description": "Validation Error", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}}, "/api/visits": {"post": {"tags": ["questions"], "summary": "Mark now as seen, for the since-last-visit filter", "description": "**Deliberately not a side effect of reading the queue.** If a GET stamped a visit, the\nnext GET would have a baseline of a moment ago and *what changed since I last looked*\nwould be permanently empty \u2014 right once, then wrong forever.", "operationId": "markVisited", "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Visited"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}, "/api/questions/answer": {"post": {"tags": ["questions"], "summary": "Settle one question on one draft", "description": "Settle one question. Three lines, because the logic is a service.\n\n**No `try`.** A `ValueError` from below carries a coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, or\nthe reason check \u2014 and `create_app` turns it into a 422 for every route at once, exactly\nas the forge does. Catching it here would be a second spelling of one contract,\nand the second spelling is the one that drifts.", "operationId": "answerQuestion", "requestBody": {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/AnswerRequest"}}}, "required": true}, "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Answered"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}, "/api/questions/answer-all": {"post": {"tags": ["questions"], "summary": "Settle one question on every draft that asks it", "description": "**A partial batch is a 200, not a 207 and not a 422.** The operation did what it was\nasked and is reporting what it found; the refusals are in the body with their codes.\nA 207 is a status no generated client models usefully.", "operationId": "answerAll", "requestBody": {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/AnswerAllRequest"}}}, "required": true}, "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/AnsweredAll"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}, "/api/questions/propose": {"post": {"tags": ["questions"], "summary": "Decline a question \u2014 nothing declared fits", "description": "Invariant 7's escape hatch. The hole stays open; `still_open` says so in the payload.", "operationId": "proposeType", "requestBody": {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/ProposeRequest"}}}, "required": true}, "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Proposed"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}, "/api/questions/proposals/decide": {"post": {"tags": ["questions"], "summary": "Approve, rename or reject a proposal", "description": "One route, not two. Approve and reject are one decision with a value, and separate\nendpoints would let them drift apart.", "operationId": "decideProposal", "requestBody": {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/DecideRequest"}}}, "required": true}, "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Decided"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}, "/api/health/registry": {"get": {"tags": ["health"], "summary": "What the registry holds, and when it was last checked", "operationId": "registryHealth", "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Strip"}}}}}}}, "/api/registry/types/{id}": {"get": {"tags": ["registry"], "summary": "A type's states, and which contracts use it", "operationId": "lookupType", "parameters": [{"name": "id", "in": "path", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string", "title": "Id"}}], "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/TypeCard"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}, "/api/contracts": {"get": {"tags": ["contracts"], "summary": "Every contract, worst first", "operationId": "listContracts", "parameters": [{"name": "against", "in": "query", "required": false, "schema": {"anyOf": [{"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Status"}, {"type": "null"}], "description": "Only this status.", "title": "Against"}, "description": "Only this status."}, {"name": "role", "in": "query", "required": false, "schema": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "description": "Only contracts with this role.", "title": "Role"}, "description": "Only contracts with this role."}, {"name": "source", "in": "query", "required": false, "schema": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "description": "Only this namespace.", "title": "Source"}, "description": "Only this namespace."}], "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Listing"}}}}, "422": {"description": "Validation Error", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}}, "/api/contracts/{id}/drift": {"get": {"tags": ["contracts"], "summary": "What moved between a contract and its source, and what it means", "operationId": "readDrift", "parameters": [{"name": "id", "in": "path", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string", "title": "Id"}}], "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/DriftReport"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}, "/api/contracts/{id}/drift/accept": {"post": {"tags": ["contracts"], "summary": "Take the source's value for one field", "operationId": "acceptDrift", "parameters": [{"name": "id", "in": "path", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string", "title": "Id"}}], "requestBody": {"required": true, "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/AcceptBody"}}}}, "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/AcceptResult"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}, "/api/contracts/{id}": {"get": {"tags": ["contracts"], "summary": "One contract, its module, and what points at it", "operationId": "readContract", "parameters": [{"name": "id", "in": "path", "required": true, "schema": {"type": "string", "title": "Id"}}], "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/ModulePage"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}, "/api/sources": {"get": {"tags": ["sources"], "summary": "What can be read, and what has been done", "operationId": "listSources", "parameters": [{"name": "state", "in": "query", "required": false, "schema": {"anyOf": [{"$ref": "#/components/schemas/State"}, {"type": "null"}], "description": "Only this state.", "title": "State"}, "description": "Only this state."}], "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Catalogue"}}}}, "422": {"description": "Validation Error", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"}}}}}}}, "/api/sources/draft": {"post": {"tags": ["sources"], "summary": "Start a draft from a source", "operationId": "draftTool", "requestBody": {"content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/DraftBody"}}}, "required": true}, "responses": {"200": {"description": "Successful Response", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/DraftResult"}}}}, "422": {"description": "A coded refusal \u2014 `MF0002`, `MF0003`, `MD\u2026`. `forge explain <code>` expands it. A malformed body also answers 422, in FastAPI's validation shape.", "content": {"application/json": {"schema": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Refusal"}}}}}}}}, "components": {"schemas": {"AcceptBody": {"properties": {"field": {"type": "string", "title": "Field"}, "by": {"type": "string", "title": "By"}, "why": {"type": "string", "title": "Why"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["field", "by", "why"], "title": "AcceptBody"}, "AcceptResult": {"properties": {"contract_id": {"type": "string", "title": "Contract Id"}, "field": {"type": "string", "title": "Field"}, "was": {"type": "string", "title": "Was"}, "now": {"type": "string", "title": "Now"}, "path": {"type": "string", "title": "Path"}, "branch": {"type": "string", "title": "Branch"}, "commit": {"type": "string", "title": "Commit"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["contract_id", "field", "was", "now", "path", "branch", "commit"], "title": "AcceptResult"}, "AnswerAllRequest": {"properties": {"subject": {"type": "string", "title": "Subject"}, "value": {"title": "Value"}, "why": {"type": "string", "title": "Why"}, "by": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "By"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["subject", "value", "why"], "title": "AnswerAllRequest"}, "AnswerRequest": {"properties": {"draft": {"type": "string", "title": "Draft"}, "subject": {"type": "string", "title": "Subject"}, "value": {"title": "Value"}, "why": {"type": "string", "title": "Why"}, "by": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "By"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["draft", "subject", "value", "why"], "title": "AnswerRequest"}, "Answered": {"properties": {"draft": {"type": "string", "title": "Draft"}, "subject": {"type": "string", "title": "Subject"}, "remaining": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Remaining"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["draft", "subject", "remaining"], "title": "Answered"}, "AnsweredAll": {"properties": {"subject": {"type": "string", "title": "Subject"}, "settled": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Settled"}, "refused": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/RefusedDraft"}, "type": "array", "title": "Refused"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["subject", "settled", "refused"], "title": "AnsweredAll"}, "Band": {"type": "string", "enum": ["drift", "routing", "cosmetic", "prose", "blocked"], "title": "Band", "description": "How much a wrong answer costs, which is not the same as how likely one is.\n\nGraded by consequence rather than hit rate \u2014 the operator's call on 2026-08-17, after\nthe forge measured a model at 97% on the fields that change which pipeline gets built\nand ~60% on port labels. A flat accuracy number averages those two and hides the only\none worth knowing."}, "Candidate": {"properties": {"value": {"type": "string", "title": "Value"}, "note": {"type": "string", "title": "Note", "default": ""}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["value"], "title": "Candidate", "description": "One thing that may be answered, and where it comes from.\n\nNot `CandidateRef` \u2014 that is `egress.py`'s alias for a *reference* that crosses door 2\n(`ContractId | EdgeRef | None`). This is the offered option a reviewer reads."}, "Catalogue": {"properties": {"rows": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/ToolRow"}, "type": "array", "title": "Rows"}, "counts": {"additionalProperties": {"type": "integer"}, "type": "object", "title": "Counts"}, "sources": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Sources"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["rows", "counts", "sources"], "title": "Catalogue"}, "ContractRow": {"properties": {"id": {"type": "string", "title": "Id"}, "roles": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Roles"}, "source": {"type": "string", "title": "Source"}, "status": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Status"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["id", "roles", "source", "status"], "title": "ContractRow"}, "DecideRequest": {"properties": {"draft": {"type": "string", "title": "Draft"}, "subject": {"type": "string", "title": "Subject"}, "decision": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Decision"}, "why": {"type": "string", "title": "Why"}, "id": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Id"}, "by": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "By"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["draft", "subject", "decision", "why"], "title": "DecideRequest"}, "Decided": {"properties": {"draft": {"type": "string", "title": "Draft"}, "subject": {"type": "string", "title": "Subject"}, "value": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Value"}, "still_open": {"type": "boolean", "title": "Still Open"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["draft", "subject", "value", "still_open"], "title": "Decided"}, "Decision": {"type": "string", "enum": ["open", "approved", "rejected"], "title": "Decision", "description": "What a reviewer said about a proposal.\n\n`OPEN` is the default because a proposal arrives undecided, and a default of anything\nelse would make an unreviewed proposal look reviewed."}, "Diagnostic": {"properties": {"code": {"type": "string", "title": "Code"}, "where": {"type": "string", "title": "Where"}, "summary": {"type": "string", "title": "Summary"}, "detail": {"type": "string", "title": "Detail"}, "fix": {"type": "string", "title": "Fix"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["code", "where", "summary", "detail", "fix"], "title": "Diagnostic"}, "DraftBody": {"properties": {"ref": {"type": "string", "title": "Ref"}, "name": {"type": "string", "title": "Name"}, "version": {"type": "string", "title": "Version"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["ref", "name", "version"], "title": "DraftBody"}, "DraftResult": {"properties": {"name": {"type": "string", "title": "Name"}, "target": {"type": "string", "title": "Target"}, "holes": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Hole"}, "type": "array", "title": "Holes"}, "filled": {"additionalProperties": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/FilledValue"}, "type": "object", "title": "Filled"}, "generated_module": {"type": "boolean", "title": "Generated Module"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["name", "target", "holes", "filled", "generated_module"], "title": "DraftResult"}, "DriftReport": {"properties": {"contract_id": {"type": "string", "title": "Contract Id"}, "verifiable": {"type": "boolean", "title": "Verifiable"}, "module_read": {"type": "boolean", "title": "Module Read"}, "checks": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/FieldCheck"}, "type": "array", "title": "Checks"}, "conformance": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Diagnostic"}, "type": "array", "title": "Conformance"}, "unchecked": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Unchecked"}, "type": "array", "title": "Unchecked"}, "verdict": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Verdict"}, "says": {"type": "string", "title": "Says"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["contract_id", "verifiable", "module_read", "checks", "conformance", "unchecked", "verdict", "says"], "title": "DriftReport"}, "Excerpt": {"properties": {"locator": {"type": "string", "title": "Locator"}, "text": {"type": "string", "title": "Text"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["locator", "text"], "title": "Excerpt", "description": "A span of source text and a resolvable pointer to it.\n\n`locator` is a `file:line` or a URL \u2014 never a bare claim. The rule drafter's \u00a73.2\nmakes the same demand of a citation for the same reason: a reviewer approving\nsomething is approving that the quoted text supports it, and they cannot do that\nwithout the text.\n\n**A file locator is relative to the root it was read under, never absolute.** An\nabsolute one carries the machine into every draft and every golden file, which is the\ndefect issue #46 found in `digest_of_directory` \u2014 and it was a golden file that caught\nit here too, on the first one written.\n\n**`text` is weaker than this docstring asks for, today.** The nf-core source sets one\nexcerpt per fact naming the process and the file rather than quoting the line the fact\nwas read from, because `ModuleSpec` records no line numbers. That is enough to find the\nevidence and not enough to read it without opening the file \u2014 a real gap, and the right\nplace to close it is `ModuleSpec`, so that conformance diagnostics gain line numbers at\nthe same time.\n\n**Moved here from the forge's `observe` module by Plan 2.5.** A build-path question that\nquotes its evidence needs the same type, and the forge is where it was first needed rather\nthan where it belongs.\n\n(Naming that module's package in full here trips `test_no_pure_package_imports_an_impure_one`,\nwhich is a substring scan over the file text rather than an import analysis. The guard is\nblunt rather than wrong, and rewording is cheaper than teaching it to read Python.)"}, "FieldCheck": {"properties": {"field": {"type": "string", "title": "Field"}, "impact": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Impact"}, "registry_says": {"type": "string", "title": "Registry Says"}, "source_says": {"type": "string", "title": "Source Says"}, "agrees": {"type": "boolean", "title": "Agrees"}, "locator": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Locator"}, "excerpt": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Excerpt"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["field", "impact", "registry_says", "source_says", "agrees", "locator", "excerpt"], "title": "FieldCheck"}, "FilledValue": {"properties": {"value": {"title": "Value"}, "by": {"type": "string", "title": "By"}, "how": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/ValueSource"}, "why": {"type": "string", "title": "Why"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["value", "by", "how", "why"], "title": "FilledValue", "description": "A settled hole. Adds nothing to `Answer` \u2014 see the spec's \u00a74.2, where that is read\nas a signal the base is drawn at about the right place.\n\n`by` is `nf-core` for a derived fact, a username for a hand fill, a model id for a\nmodel one. `land` copies it verbatim into `Provenance.drafted_by`."}, "Grouping": {"type": "string", "enum": ["question", "module"], "title": "Grouping"}, "HTTPValidationError": {"properties": {"detail": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/ValidationError"}, "type": "array", "title": "Detail"}}, "type": "object", "title": "HTTPValidationError"}, "Hole": {"properties": {"subject": {"type": "string", "title": "Subject"}, "what": {"type": "string", "title": "What", "default": ""}, "why_open": {"type": "string", "title": "Why Open", "default": ""}, "candidates": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Candidate"}, "type": "array", "title": "Candidates"}, "closed": {"type": "boolean", "title": "Closed", "default": true}, "evidence": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Excerpt"}, "type": "array", "title": "Evidence"}, "after": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "After"}, "channels": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Channels", "default": []}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["subject"], "title": "Hole", "description": "An unanswered question about a contract being drafted.\n\n**The blocking lives in `Scaffold`, not here.** `Scaffold.is_complete()` gates\n`contract_from`, so the forge cannot emit an invalid declared file. Putting that on\nthis class \u2014 as a field or as a method \u2014 would trade a structural guarantee for a\nruntime check on a value, which is the mistake `CLAUDE.md` records about invariant 1."}, "Impact": {"type": "string", "enum": ["routes", "builds", "records"], "title": "Impact", "description": "What reads this field \u2014 which is what decides how much a change to it matters."}, "Listing": {"properties": {"rows": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/ContractRow"}, "type": "array", "title": "Rows"}, "total": {"type": "integer", "title": "Total"}, "counts": {"additionalProperties": {"type": "integer"}, "type": "object", "title": "Counts"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["rows", "total", "counts"], "title": "Listing"}, "ModulePage": {"properties": {"id": {"type": "string", "title": "Id"}, "roles": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Roles"}, "container": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Container"}, "consumes": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Port"}, "type": "array", "title": "Consumes"}, "produces": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Port"}, "type": "array", "title": "Produces"}, "source_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Source Path"}, "emits_total": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Emits Total"}, "emits_declared": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Emits Declared"}, "rules_aiming": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Rules Aiming"}, "inputs_from": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Inputs From"}, "outputs_feed": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Outputs Feed"}, "competes_with": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Competes With"}, "pipeline_pins": {"type": "null", "title": "Pipeline Pins"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["id", "roles", "container", "consumes", "produces", 