ecided Why", "default": ""}, "decided_id": {"type": "string", "title": "Decided Id", "default": ""}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["id", "description", "why", "by"], "title": "Proposal", "description": "What a hole needs that the vocabulary cannot express yet.\n\n**Not a fill.** A hole with a proposal stays open: `is_complete()` is still false and\n`contract_from` still refuses, because a contract whose port cites an undeclared type is\nthe load-time refusal invariant 7 already makes. What a proposal changes is that the hole\nnow says *why* it is open \u2014 \"nothing declared fits, and here is what would\" \u2014 rather than\nlooking like a field nobody has reached.\n\n**Not a vocabulary file either.** It lives in the workspace draft. Nothing writes\n`vocabularies/`; a person moves it, which is invariant 2's approval step and the whole of\nwhat bounds a model inventing an id and a sentence.\n\nSee `notes/specs/2026-08-17-vocabulary-proposals.md`."}, "ProposeRequest": {"properties": {"draft": {"type": "string", "title": "Draft"}, "subject": {"type": "string", "title": "Subject"}, "id": {"type": "string", "title": "Id"}, "description": {"type": "string", "title": "Description"}, "why": {"type": "string", "title": "Why"}, "by": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "By"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["draft", "subject", "id", "description", "why"], "title": "ProposeRequest"}, "Proposed": {"properties": {"draft": {"type": "string", "title": "Draft"}, "subject": {"type": "string", "title": "Subject"}, "still_open": {"type": "boolean", "title": "Still Open"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["draft", "subject", "still_open"], "title": "Proposed"}, "QueueResponse": {"properties": {"questions": {"items": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/OpenQuestion"}, "type": "array", "title": "Questions"}, "total": {"type": "integer", "title": "Total"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["questions", "total"], "title": "QueueResponse"}, "Refusal": {"properties": {"detail": {"type": "string", "title": "Detail"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["detail"], "title": "Refusal", "description": "A coded refusal. `detail` is `\"<code>: <message>\"` \u2014 `forge explain <code>` expands it."}, "RefusedDraft": {"properties": {"draft": {"type": "string", "title": "Draft"}, "detail": {"type": "string", "title": "Detail"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["draft", "detail"], "title": "RefusedDraft"}, "RowKind": {"type": "string", "enum": ["question", "drift"], "title": "RowKind", "description": "What a row IS, which decides where following it leads.\n\nOne row shape for every kind of work is firm (design \u00a78), and a row still has to know\nwhether it leads to a question or to a contract. Derived nowhere and stored here because\nit is a fact about the row's origin rather than about its content."}, "State": {"type": "string", "enum": ["undrafted", "drafted", "landed"], "title": "State"}, "Status": {"type": "string", "enum": ["drifted", "unverifiable", "matching"], "title": "Status"}, "Strip": {"properties": {"contracts": {"type": "integer", "title": "Contracts"}, "matching": {"type": "integer", "title": "Matching"}, "unverifiable": {"type": "integer", "title": "Unverifiable"}, "types": {"type": "integer", "title": "Types"}, "checked_at": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string", "format": "date-time"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Checked At"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["contracts", "matching", "unverifiable", "types", "checked_at"], "title": "Strip"}, "ToolRow": {"properties": {"ref": {"type": "string", "title": "Ref"}, "state": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/State"}, "contract_id": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Contract Id"}, "draft": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "title": "Draft"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["ref", "state"], "title": "ToolRow"}, "TypeCard": {"properties": {"id": {"type": "string", "title": "Id"}, "states": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "States"}, "produced_by": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Produced By"}, "consumed_by": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array", "title": "Consumed By"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["id", "states", "produced_by", "consumed_by"], "title": "TypeCard"}, "Unchecked": {"properties": {"field": {"type": "string", "title": "Field"}, "impact": {"$ref": "#/components/schemas/Impact"}, "why": {"type": "string", "title": "Why"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "type": "object", "required": ["field", "impact", "why"], "title": "Unchecked"}, "ValidationError": {"properties": {"loc": {"items": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "integer"}]}, "type": "array", "title": "Location"}, "msg": {"type": "string", "title": "Message"}, "type": {"type": "string", "title": "Error Type"}, "input": {"title": "Input"}, "ctx": {"type": "object", "title": "Context"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["loc", "msg", "type"], "title": "ValidationError"}, "ValueSource": {"type": "string", "enum": ["resolver", "goal", "human", "model", "measured", "derived"], "title": "ValueSource", "description": "Who decided a value, recorded separately from how well it was decided.\n\nA tier says *how* something was settled; it should not also have to say *who*. A user\nwho pins a parameter has legitimately removed the ambiguity, so the tier is still\nstructural \u2014 but a reviewer needs to see that Mendel did not derive it. Same shape as\nmeasured-versus-asserted in the profiling spec, and for the same reason.\n\n**Not `PremiseOrigin`, which also has a `DERIVED`.** That enum answers *how good is this\nas evidence*; this one answers *who settled it*. Its own docstring draws the same line,\nand the two `DERIVED`s mean different things: there, a fact computed from other facts;\nhere, a fact read straight off a source file."}, "Verdict": {"type": "string", "enum": ["breaks", "reroutes", "rebuilds", "recorded", "agrees"], "title": "Verdict", "description": "The only question a maintainer really has, answered \u2014 design \u00a77."}, "Visited": {"properties": {"seen_at": {"type": "string", "format": "date-time", "title": "Seen At"}}, "type": "object", "required": ["seen_at"], "title": "Visited"}}}, "tags": [{"name": "questions", "description": "What is open, and how it gets closed."}, {"name": "health", "description": "Whether the service is up, and what the registry holds."}, {"name": "registry", "description": "The declared data, read only."}, {"name": "contracts", "description": "What has landed. Read only."}, {"name": "sources", "description": "What can be read, and starting a draft."}]}
